7592186395774 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395777 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395774 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395778 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395774 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395779 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395774 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395774 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395774 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395779 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395774 1080 #uuid "2332d85e-5e88-505c-b823-5f0ae7f57fb3" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395775 1081 "Other" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395775 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395775 1084 #uuid "b3993775-0f8e-5c7e-b158-1a52fe75de99" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395776 1081 "Identity matrix" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395776 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395776 1084 #uuid "d4aa5d0b-3502-5db7-982d-257ca9d0ebb8" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395777 1081 "Lower triangular matrix" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395777 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395777 1084 #uuid "9c6da7fb-8eba-5ffa-9bde-d1144a8dbb47" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395778 1081 "Diagonal matrix" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395778 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395778 1084 #uuid "7bc5b9ce-5da0-55fe-8e2a-df8eb4ecfc52" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395779 1081 "Upper triangular matrix" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395779 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395779 1084 #uuid "6657fbe8-1958-5cc4-b147-eb6c679992c6" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395780 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395781 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395780 1069 "q-13912" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395780 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395780 1071 "Find the radius of convergence $R$ and interval of convergence $I$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395780 1072 #uuid "4c54e973-6e64-50b6-b096-4b16776e42ab" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395780 1074 "To apply the ratio test we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x-1)^{3(n+1)}}{(n+1)^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{n}^{3}}{(x-1)^{3n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{n}^{3}(x-1)^{3}}{(n+1)^{3}}| \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n}{n+1})}^{3} \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-1{|}^{3} & <1 \\\\ |x-1| & <1 \\\\ -1<x-1 & <1 \\\\ 0<x & <2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the radius of convergence is $R=1,$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(0,2).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x-1|=1,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=0$ and $x=2$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\n- When $x=2$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(2-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis series is convergent by the $p$-series test.\n\nConsequently, the interval of convergence is $I=[0,2].$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395782 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395783 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395784 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395785 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395786 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395785 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395781 1080 #uuid "bdf61ccf-2627-5fa3-a051-531ba920ddff" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395782 1081 "$R=1$ and  $I=(0,2]$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395782 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395782 1084 #uuid "71cb4bda-fc1e-5f5c-a387-81bc7f680311" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395783 1081 "$R=\\infty $ and  $I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395783 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395783 1084 #uuid "c5872ac5-73b0-58bc-a4ce-df051df3c8ad" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395784 1081 "$R=1$ and  $I=[0,2)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395784 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395784 1084 #uuid "de6804fa-3d4a-5001-8f45-18bc86c68bd6" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395785 1081 "$R=1$ and  $I=[0,2]$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395785 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395785 1084 #uuid "a52347ba-5949-5d61-b02a-567dd46a130d" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395786 1081 "$R=1$ and  $I=(0,2)$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395786 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395786 1084 #uuid "f635175f-1efc-5299-8c7e-5584974b36e7" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395788 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1069 "q-14050" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1071 "![](images/04/0470661491c0d9d44ecbbc3c87af70d4ff334f1ffd2ca56b68bd4c126f3d88de.png)\n\nWhat are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1072 #uuid "1270303e-0109-58be-ac65-6aecbfb8540f" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395787 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(3,-4)$ and passes through the point $(0,-\\frac{7}{4}).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(3,-4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4p(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(0,-\\frac{7}{4}),$ we substitute $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{7}{4}$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-3)^{2} & =4p(-\\frac{7}{4}+4) \\\\ 9 & =4p(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =4(0+4) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $7$ and $-1.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395789 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395790 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395791 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395792 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395793 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1077 "selection" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395790 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395788 1080 #uuid "1984d219-413d-5333-ac39-1acd7d9d0ec5" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1081 "$8$ and $-1$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395789 1084 #uuid "fbcf88a3-1e20-5a4c-bb86-1fe1bdaa1963" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1081 "$7$ and $-1$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395790 1084 #uuid "ae0d6ea0-c5ed-5e7f-9687-ab98aef0c28b" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395791 1081 "$9$ and $-2$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395791 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395791 1084 #uuid "c4dc7a4e-aacb-5122-89ac-d5eb5d04a7da" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395792 1081 "$7$ and $-2$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395792 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395792 1084 #uuid "950ec668-d2b7-5d89-8e4f-1d349b1209a4" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395793 1081 "$8$ and $-3$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395793 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395793 1084 #uuid "2789771c-579f-5375-8680-854defcdf4d4" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395794 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395795 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395794 1069 "q-14241" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395794 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395794 1071 "![](images/9b/9b7acbd4f24b6bbd20dd00fc042405324c069d28db0102c2cd7dd49e6b3bbccd.png)\n\nWhat are the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395794 1072 #uuid "0ecc876e-1e30-5d04-b02b-e0d45341e6f7" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395794 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,4)$ and passes through the point $(-6,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(2,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-6,8),$ we substitute $x=-6$ and $y=8$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8-4)^{2} & =4p(-6-2) \\\\ 16 & =4p(-8) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =-2(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =-2(0-2) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2+4 \\\\ y & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $2$ and  $6.$" 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395796 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395797 13194139533466 17592186045585 true] [17592186395795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395798 1319413953